he foundation upon which the Freehold exists and was created. Yes, it exists as the main bulwark, but is also heavily linked with the legends of the Fountain of Youth, and carries significant symbology to the court. Flames are a source of death and rebirth, and yet, despite evolving and changing over the years, the Freehold continues dragging on an unnatural existence, as the Flames are fed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:53:58-08:00","id":1036258,"title":"","content":"The Ocean Court tends to present a very laid back and casual face, but everyone in the Freehold knows they will violently protect the peace and, in many cases, the status quo. They originate from the Reconstruction era of the American South.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12873-thatxygirl","name":"thatxygirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}